**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**How to implement.** The identities, the provenance and the name rule of the library-entry files, in Domain (001 §A; 001 §B 'Every entry file carries'; .spec-md §3.11, §5). New `OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryEntryFiles.fs`: `module LibraryEntryFiles` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Domain`, compiled directly after `ElementId.fs` (one `<Compile>` line right after `ElementId.fs`'s in `OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj`) and with no new comment. It opens `MaterialLibrary`, `Library`, `Placement` and `Softellect.Sys.Primitives` (`FileName`, `FileExtension`). Every type follows `AGENTS.md`: single-case unions carry `.value`, case names have two words, no `bool` appears, and each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050. (1) `LibraryEntryKind`: `MaterialEntryKind`, `SampleEntryKind`, `SourceEntryKind`, `PolarizerEntryKind`, `DetectorEntryKind` and `CategoryEntryKind` (S7.1 adds the item-model kind). `member value : int` answers 1 to 6 in that order, and `static member tryOfWire (v : int) : LibraryEntryKind option` answers `None` for any other tag. `member extension : FileExtension` answers `.material-json`, `.sample-json`, `.source-json`, `.polarizer-json`, `.detector-json` and `.category-json` (001 §A). `member currentSchemaVersion : FileSchemaVersion` answers 1 for every kind. `static member all : LibraryEntryKind list` lists the six in tag order. (2) `FileSchemaVersion of int` is the schema version a stored file declares, and `EntrySchema = { kind : LibraryEntryKind; version : FileSchemaVersion }`. (3) `LibraryEntryId of Guid` is an entry's frozen GUID, whatever its kind (001 §B 'Identity is GUID + version + hash'). Type extensions after it: `MaterialId.toLibraryEntryId`, `SampleId.toLibraryEntryId` and `CategoryId.toLibraryEntryId` keep the GUID. `ElementValueId.tryToLibraryEntryId : LibraryEntryId option` parses a preset's id and answers `None` for any other text; since step 20, every seeded and minted preset id is the canonical string of a GUID. No conversion goes the other way (ELEV006): step 25's decoders build a kind's id at the file seam. (4) `CatalogueId of Guid`, `CatalogueName of string` and `KitId of Guid`. `KitId` is the GUID a kit's `.kit-json` carries (001 §E). The provenance needs it now, so it is born here, and S4.1's `Kit` module MUST reuse this type rather than declare a second one (ELEV014). (5) Provenance (001 §B): `MaterialSourceName`, `MaterialSourceRecordId`, `MaterialSourceVersion`, `EntryLicence` (an SPDX identifier, e.g. `CC0-1.0` or `CC-BY-4.0`) and `EntryCitation`, each `of string`; `SourcePullInfo = { source : MaterialSourceName; record : MaterialSourceRecordId; sourceVersion : MaterialSourceVersion; licence : EntryLicence; citation : EntryCitation }`; and `EntryProvenance` = `BuiltInProvenance of CatalogueId` | `UserProvenance` | `KitImportProvenance of KitId` | `SourcePullProvenance of SourcePullInfo`. A built-in's protection derives from its provenance: `member protection : EntryProtection` answers `ProtectedBuiltIn` for `BuiltInProvenance` and `UserManaged` for the rest, and `member categoryOrigin : CategoryOrigin` answers `BuiltInCategory` or `UserCategory` by the same rule. (6) `ContentHash of string` is the lowercase hex SHA-256 of an entry's canonical content. Storage computes it (step 27). (7) The name rule (001 §A; .spec-md §3.11) is `FileStem of string`. `static member ofText (text : string) : FileStem` replaces each of `: * ? " < > |` and the separators `/` and `\` with `_` and keeps every other character. `member withExtension (extension : FileExtension) : FileName` answers the stem followed by the extension. `EntryName.fileStem : FileStem` is a type extension. No reserved-name, length or trimming rule is added. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs` (`module LibraryEntryFilesTests`), appended to the compile list after `CanonicalJsonTests.fs`. (a) `every library entry kind round-trips its wire tag and renders its 001 extension`: the six tags in order, `tryOfWire` inverse to `value`, `None` for 0 and 7, the six extensions exactly as above, version 1 and `all` in tag order. (b) `a file stem keeps the name's characters and replaces only the ones Windows forbids`: `Ti:sapphire laser, tunable 700–1000 nm` becomes `Ti_sapphire laser, tunable 700–1000 nm`; `a/b\c*d?e"f<g>h|i:j` becomes `a_b_c_d_e_f_g_h_i_j`; `Langasite (La3Ga5SiO14)` and `CO₂ laser 10.6 µm` are unchanged; and `(EntryName "Silicon").fileStem.withExtension MaterialEntryKind.extension` is `FileName "Silicon.material-json"`. (c) `a built-in provenance is protected and every other provenance is user-managed`: `protection` and `categoryOrigin` of each of the four provenance cases. (d) `a library entry id keeps the GUID of the kind's own id`: `MaterialIds.silicon`, `SampleIds.multilayerQwId` and `CategoryIds.glass` keep their GUIDs; `PresetIds.detectorEllipsometer.tryToLibraryEntryId` is the GUID its text spells; and a test-local non-GUID `ElementValueId` answers `None`.

**Acceptance.** After `LibraryEntryFiles.fs` lands, constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `every library entry kind round-trips its wire tag and renders its 001 extension`, `a file stem keeps the name's characters and replaces only the ones Windows forbids`, `a built-in provenance is protected and every other provenance is user-managed` and `a library entry id keeps the GUID of the kind's own id`; and build, elevation, constructor-unit-tests and the six s04 invariants MUST pass.
